$ Sample: strut-braced engine pylon on a minimal wing (SOL 101)  — issue #38
$
$ A cantilever wing stick (5 CBARs along +Y), a vertical CBAR pylon spine from the
$ mid-span grid down to the engine grid, and two triangulated rod struts from the
$ neighbouring wing grids to the engine. One strut is a CROD (+PROD), the other the
$ same section written inline as a CONROD. The engine is a CONM2.
$
$ Geometry (m):  wing root grid 1 at the origin, grids 2-6 at y = 1..5
$                engine grid 20 at (0, 2, -1.2); spine 3 -> 20; struts 2 -> 20, 4 -> 20
$ Material:      aluminium  E = 7.1e10, G = 2.7e10, rho = 2800
$ Sections:      wing  PBAR 1  A = 0.02,  I1 = 2.0e-4, I2 = 2.0e-5, J = 1.0e-4
$                spine PBAR 2  A = 0.004, I1 = I2 = 2.0e-6,        J = 4.0e-6
$                strut PROD 3  A = 5.0e-4, J = 1.0e-7, C = 5.0e-3 (CONROD 22 inline)
$ Engine:        CONM2 100, m = 250 kg at grid 20
$ Loads:         GRAV 20  1 g in -Z;  FORCE 30  thrust 4000 N in +X at the engine
$                LOAD 100 = 1g + thrust (subcase 1); 1g alone (subcase 2)
$
$ Rod-only grids need their free rotations SPC'd (no AUTOSPC in sbeam). Here the
$ engine grid is also the spine's end B, so it needs none.
$ Gated in tests/integration/test_sample_verification.py (free body of the engine
$ grid: strut forces + spine end-B force + applied load = 0; reactions = -applied).
$ Units: SI (m, N, kg, Pa)
$
SOL 101
$
SUBCASE 1
  TITLE        = Pylon struts — 1g + thrust
  SPC          = 1
  LOAD         = 100
  DISPLACEMENT = ALL
  SPCFORCE     = ALL
  FORCE        = ALL
  STRESS       = ALL
$
SUBCASE 2
  TITLE        = Pylon struts — 1g
  SPC          = 1
  LOAD         = 20
  DISPLACEMENT = ALL
  SPCFORCE     = ALL
  FORCE        = ALL
  STRESS       = ALL
$
BEGIN BULK
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------ NODES
GRID,  1, , 0.0, 0.0, 0.0
GRID,  2, , 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
GRID,  3, , 0.0, 2.0, 0.0
GRID,  4, , 0.0, 3.0, 0.0
GRID,  5, , 0.0, 4.0, 0.0
GRID,  6, , 0.0, 5.0, 0.0
GRID, 20, , 0.0, 2.0, -1.2
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------- MATERIAL
MAT1, 1, 7.1e10, 2.7e10, 0.33, 2800.0
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------- PROPERTIES
PBAR, 1, 1, 0.02,  2.0e-4, 2.0e-5, 1.0e-4
PBAR, 2, 1, 0.004, 2.0e-6, 2.0e-6, 4.0e-6
PROD, 3, 1, 5.0e-4, 1.0e-7, 5.0e-3
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------- ELEMENTS
$ Wing: element y-axis = global -X (so local z = global Z is the lift direction)
CBAR,  1, 1, 1, 2, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR,  2, 1, 2, 3, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR,  3, 1, 3, 4, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR,  4, 1, 4, 5, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR,  5, 1, 5, 6, -1.0, 0.0, 0.0
$ Pylon spine, vertical, element y-axis = global X
CBAR, 10, 2, 3, 20, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
$ Struts: a CROD and the same section as a CONROD
CROD,   21, 3, 2, 20
CONROD, 22, 4, 20, 1, 5.0e-4, 1.0e-7, 5.0e-3
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------- MASS
CONM2, 100, 20, 0, 250.0
$
$ ----------------------------------------------------------- CONSTRAINTS
SPC1, 1, 123456, 1
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------ LOADS
GRAV,  20, 0, 9.81, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0
FORCE, 30, 20, 0, 4000.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
LOAD, 100, 1.0, 1.0, 20, 1.0, 30
$
ENDDATA
